§ `The dates module`

-- 31 January plus one month: February 2025 has no 31st, so its last day (fork F2).
#ASSERT `31 Jan 2025` `plus calendar months` 1 EQUALS `28 Feb 2025`
-- 29 February 2024 plus 12 months: 28 February 2025 (fork F2).
#ASSERT `29 Feb 2024` `plus calendar months` 12 EQUALS `28 Feb 2025`
#ASSERT `15 Mar 2024` `plus calendar months` 24 EQUALS `15 Mar 2026`
#ASSERT `1 Oct 2026` `plus days` 60 EQUALS `30 Nov 2026`
#ASSERT `the number of days from` `1 Oct 2026` `until` `1 Dec 2026` EQUALS 61

§ `s 3(1) -- unlawful discrimination`

`UD PART` MEANS `yes: acts, omissions or practices unlawful under that Part are unlawful discrimination (s 3(1))`
`UD OFFENCE` MEANS `yes: conduct that is an offence under that Division is included in unlawful discrimination (s 3(1))`
`UD EXCLUDED` MEANS `no: that offence is expressly left out of unlawful discrimination (s 3(1), "other than": the text's no)`
`UD OTHER LAW` MEANS `no: unlawful discrimination means only what is unlawful under the four Acts and Parts listed in s 3(1) (a "means" definition: the text's no)`

`ADA Part 4` MEANS `Part 4 of the Age Discrimination Act 2004`
`DDA Part 2` MEANS `Division 1, 2, 2A, 3 or 6 of Part 2 of the Disability Discrimination Act 1992`
`RDA` MEANS `Part II or IIA of the Racial Discrimination Act 1975`
`SDA` MEANS `Part II of the Sex Discrimination Act 1984`
`ADA offence` MEANS `an offence under Division 2 of Part 5 of the Age Discrimination Act 2004, other than s 51 or s 52`
`DDA offence` MEANS `an offence under Division 4 of Part 2 of the Disability Discrimination Act 1992, other than s 42`
`excluded offence` MEANS `an offence under s 51 or s 52 of the Age Discrimination Act 2004, or s 42 of the Disability Discrimination Act 1992`
`other law` MEANS `another law only (for example a State or Territory discrimination law, or the Fair Work Act 2009)`

#ASSERT `s 3 -- is it unlawful discrimination` `ADA Part 4` EQUALS `UD PART`
#ASSERT `s 3 -- is it unlawful discrimination` `DDA Part 2` EQUALS `UD PART`
#ASSERT `s 3 -- is it unlawful discrimination` `RDA` EQUALS `UD PART`
#ASSERT `s 3 -- is it unlawful discrimination` `SDA` EQUALS `UD PART`
#ASSERT `s 3 -- is it unlawful discrimination` `ADA offence` EQUALS `UD OFFENCE`
#ASSERT `s 3 -- is it unlawful discrimination` `DDA offence` EQUALS `UD OFFENCE`
#ASSERT `s 3 -- is it unlawful discrimination` `excluded offence` EQUALS `UD EXCLUDED`
#ASSERT `s 3 -- is it unlawful discrimination` `other law` EQUALS `UD OTHER LAW`

§ `ss 46P, 46PB -- may I lodge this complaint`

`me only` MEANS `I am aggrieved and lodge it for myself only`
`me and others` MEANS `I am aggrieved and lodge it for myself and other people also aggrieved`
`several of us` MEANS `I am one of 2 or more aggrieved people lodging it together, for ourselves only`
`several of us and others` MEANS `I am one of 2 or more aggrieved people lodging it together, for ourselves and other people also aggrieved`
`a union for others` MEANS `I lodge it, as a person or a trade union, for one or more other people who are aggrieved`
`nobody aggrieved` MEANS `I lodge it, but neither I nor anyone it is lodged for is aggrieved`

`L YES` MEANS `yes: you may lodge it with the Commission, which must refer it to the President (ss 46P, 46PD)`
`L REP YES` MEANS `yes: you may lodge it as a representative complaint, without the class members' consent (ss 46P, 46PB(4)); the Commission must refer it to the President (s 46PD)`
`L CLASS MEMBER` MEANS `no: as a class member of a representative complaint you are not entitled to lodge a separate complaint about the same subject matter (s 46P(3), the text's no)`
`L NOT UD` MEANS `no: it must allege unlawful discrimination, which s 3(1) defines (s 46P(1)(b), a "means" definition: the text's no)`
`L NOT LISTED` MEANS `s 46P(2) does not list you: a complaint is lodged by or for a person aggrieved (NOTHING-kind)`
`L NOT WRITTEN` MEANS `not yet: the complaint must be in writing (s 46P(1)); if you need help to put it in writing the Commission must take reasonable steps to help you (s 46P(4)) (NOTHING-kind)`
`L NOT ARGUABLE` MEANS `no: it must be reasonably arguable that what you allege is unlawful discrimination (s 46P(1A), the text's no: fork F1)`
`L NO DETAILS` MEANS `not as it stands: the complaint must set out the details of what was done as fully as practicable (s 46P(1B), the text's no: fork F1)`
`L REP CONDITIONS` MEANS `no: a representative complaint may be lodged only if the class members complain against the same person, of the same, similar or related circumstances, with a substantial common issue of law or fact (s 46PB(1), "only if": the text's no)`
`L REP FORM` MEANS `not as it stands: a representative complaint must identify the class members and specify their complaints and the relief sought (s 46PB(2), the text's no: fork F1)`

-- Arguments: who, where, in writing, reasonably arguable, details set out, already a class member, same respondent,
-- related circumstances, common issue, class described.
-- A worker sacked at 63 because of age, lodging for herself: may lodge.
#ASSERT `ss 46P, 46PB -- may I lodge this complaint` `me only` `ADA Part 4` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `L YES`
-- Two employees together, for themselves only: not a representative complaint (no one else), so the s 46PB facts do not matter.
#ASSERT `ss 46P, 46PB -- may I lodge this complaint` `several of us` `SDA` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `L YES`
-- A union for a group of members, all conditions met: a representative complaint.
#ASSERT `ss 46P, 46PB -- may I lodge this complaint` `a union for others` `RDA` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `L REP YES`
#ASSERT `ss 46P, 46PB -- may I lodge this complaint` `me and others` `DDA Part 2` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `L REP YES`
#ASSERT `ss 46P, 46PB -- may I lodge this complaint` `several of us and others` `SDA` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `L REP YES`
-- Representative, but the class complain against different employers: s 46PB(1)(a) fails.
#ASSERT `ss 46P, 46PB -- may I lodge this complaint` `a union for others` `RDA` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `L REP CONDITIONS`
-- Representative, no substantial common issue: s 46PB(1)(c) fails.
#ASSERT `ss 46P, 46PB -- may I lodge this complaint` `me and others` `SDA` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `L REP CONDITIONS`
-- Representative, conditions met but the class and relief not described: s 46PB(2).
#ASSERT `ss 46P, 46PB -- may I lodge this complaint` `a union for others` `RDA` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `L REP FORM`
-- Already a class member of a representative complaint about the same subject matter: s 46P(3).
#ASSERT `ss 46P, 46PB -- may I lodge this complaint` `me only` `ADA Part 4` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `L CLASS MEMBER`
-- Unlawful only under a State law: not unlawful discrimination.
#ASSERT `ss 46P, 46PB -- may I lodge this complaint` `me only` `other law` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `L NOT UD`
-- An excluded offence (ADA s 51 victimisation as an offence).
#ASSERT `ss 46P, 46PB -- may I lodge this complaint` `me only` `excluded offence` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `L NOT UD`
#ASSERT `ss 46P, 46PB -- may I lodge this complaint` `nobody aggrieved` `SDA` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `L NOT LISTED`
#ASSERT `ss 46P, 46PB -- may I lodge this complaint` `me only` `SDA` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `L NOT WRITTEN`
#ASSERT `ss 46P, 46PB -- may I lodge this complaint` `me only` `SDA` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `L NOT ARGUABLE`
#ASSERT `ss 46P, 46PB -- may I lodge this complaint` `me only` `SDA` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `L NO DETAILS`

§ `s 46P(4) -- help to write the complaint`

#ASSERT `s 46P(4) -- must the Commission help me write my complaint` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 46P(4) -- must the Commission help me write my complaint` TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 46P(4) -- must the Commission help me write my complaint` FALSE TRUE))

§ `ss 46PA, 46PF(3), (4) -- amending`

`A YES` MEANS `yes: with the President's leave you may amend it at any time before it is terminated (s 46PA(1))`
`A ADD` MEANS `yes: with the President's leave you may amend it to add as a respondent a person alleged to have done the acts (s 46PF(3))`
`A TERMINATED` MEANS `no: a complaint cannot be amended after the President terminates it (s 46PF(4), the text's no)`
`A NO LEAVE` MEANS `not without the President's leave: ss 46PA and 46PF(3) give the power with leave, and do not limit any other power to amend (s 46PA(2)) (NOTHING-kind)`

#ASSERT `ss 46PA, 46PF -- may I amend my complaint` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `A YES`
#ASSERT `ss 46PA, 46PF -- may I amend my complaint` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `A ADD`
#ASSERT `ss 46PA, 46PF -- may I amend my complaint` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `A NO LEAVE`
-- After termination, even with leave: cannot.
#ASSERT `ss 46PA, 46PF -- may I amend my complaint` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `A TERMINATED`
#ASSERT `ss 46PA, 46PF -- may I amend my complaint` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `A TERMINATED`

§ `s 46PG -- withdrawing`

#ASSERT `s 46PG -- may I withdraw my complaint` TRUE EQUALS `yes: the President must give leave to withdraw, as all the affected persons agree (s 46PG(2)); a withdrawn complaint cannot go to court under s 46PO`
#ASSERT `s 46PG -- may I withdraw my complaint` FALSE EQUALS `no: the President cannot give leave to withdraw unless satisfied that all the affected persons agree (s 46PG(2), the text's no)`

§ `s 46PC(1) -- leaving a representative complaint`

`W YES` MEANS `yes: you may withdraw from the representative complaint by written notice to the Commission (s 46PC(1)); you may then lodge your own complaint`
`W TOO LATE` MEANS `no: a class member may withdraw only before the President terminates the complaint (s 46PC(1), a period the text fixes: the text's no)`
`W NO NOTICE` MEANS `not yet: withdrawal is by notice in writing to the Commission (s 46PC(1)) (NOTHING-kind)`

#ASSERT `s 46PC -- may I withdraw from the representative complaint` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `W YES`
#ASSERT `s 46PC -- may I withdraw from the representative complaint` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `W NO NOTICE`
#ASSERT `s 46PC -- may I withdraw from the representative complaint` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `W TOO LATE`

§ `s 46PE -- complaint against the Commission`

`E YES` MEANS `yes: the President must terminate it and notify you with reasons (s 46PE(2), (3)); you may then apply to the court (s 46PO)`
`E NOT APPLY` MEANS `no: s 46PE applies only to a complaint against the President, the Commission or a Commissioner (s 46PE(1), "if": the text's no)`
`E NO` MEANS `no: s 46PE(2) requires termination only on a complainant's written request, with the President satisfied that all the affected persons agree (s 46PE(2), "if": the text's no)`

#ASSERT `s 46PE -- must my complaint against the Commission be ended` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `E YES`
#ASSERT `s 46PE -- must my complaint against the Commission be ended` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `E NO`
#ASSERT `s 46PE -- must my complaint against the Commission be ended` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `E NO`
#ASSERT `s 46PE -- must my complaint against the Commission be ended` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `E NOT APPLY`

§ `s 46PF -- what the President does`

`F WITHOUT INQUIRY` MEANS `terminated without inquiry: the President must notify you in writing with reasons, and you may apply to the court (ss 46PF(1)(b), (1B), 46PO)`
`F UNDER 46PH` MEANS `terminated under s 46PH: the President must notify you in writing with reasons, and you may apply to the court (ss 46PH(2), 46PO)`
`F MAY STOP` MEANS `the President may decide not to inquire, or not to continue, as you do not want an inquiry or the complaint is settled or resolved (s 46PF(5))`
`F INQUIRE` MEANS `the President must inquire into your complaint and attempt to conciliate it (s 46PF(1)(c))`

#ASSERT `s 46PF -- what will the President do with my complaint` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `F INQUIRE`
#ASSERT `s 46PF -- what will the President do with my complaint` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `F WITHOUT INQUIRY`
#ASSERT `s 46PF -- what will the President do with my complaint` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `F UNDER 46PH`
#ASSERT `s 46PF -- what will the President do with my complaint` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `F MAY STOP`
#ASSERT `s 46PF -- what will the President do with my complaint` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `F MAY STOP`

-- s 46PF(10)(b): 12 months after referral.
#ASSERT `s 46PF(10) -- the 12-month target for finishing my complaint` `7 Nov 2026` EQUALS `7 Nov 2027`
-- Referred on 29 February 2024: 28 February 2025 (fork F2).
#ASSERT `s 46PF(10) -- the 12-month target for finishing my complaint` `29 Feb 2024` EQUALS `28 Feb 2025`

`N YES` MEANS `yes: the President must notify the respondent as soon as the President decides to inquire (s 46PF(7)(a), (8)(a))`
`N SAFETY` MEANS `no: the President need not notify the respondent, being satisfied that notification would be likely to prejudice a person's safety (s 46PF(7)(a), "unless": fork F3)`
`N NOT YET` MEANS `not yet: the duty to notify the respondent arises only once the President has decided to inquire (s 46PF(7), "if": the text's no)`

#ASSERT `s 46PF(7) -- will the respondent be told of my complaint` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `N YES`
#ASSERT `s 46PF(7) -- will the respondent be told of my complaint` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `N SAFETY`
#ASSERT `s 46PF(7) -- will the respondent be told of my complaint` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `N NOT YET`
#ASSERT `s 46PF(7) -- will the respondent be told of my complaint` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `N NOT YET`

§ `ss 46PI, 46PM, 46PN -- information`

`I COMPLIED` MEANS `you complied: you gave it within the period the notice specified (s 46PI(2))`
`I MUST` MEANS `you must give it: the period the notice specifies has not yet ended (s 46PI(2)); refusing or failing is an offence of 10 penalty units unless you have a reasonable excuse (s 46PM)`
`I EXCUSE` MEANS `no offence: you have a reasonable excuse (s 46PM(1A)); refusing because the answer or document might incriminate you or expose you to a penalty is one (s 46PM(3))`
`I OFFENCE` MEANS `an offence: you refused or failed to give it within the period the notice specified, without reasonable excuse (s 46PM(1)); penalty 10 penalty units`
`I NO DUTY` MEANS `no duty under s 46PM: it applies only when the President has required the information by written notice under s 46PI (s 46PM(1), "when": the text's no)`

-- Arguments: served, days in notice, given, days since service, reasonable excuse, self-incrimination.
-- A 14-day notice; given on day 14, the last day: in time.
#ASSERT `ss 46PI, 46PM -- must I give the information` TRUE 14 TRUE 14 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `I COMPLIED`
#ASSERT `ss 46PI, 46PM -- must I give the information` TRUE 14 TRUE 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `I COMPLIED`
-- Given on day 15: late, no excuse: an offence.
#ASSERT `ss 46PI, 46PM -- must I give the information` TRUE 14 TRUE 15 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `I OFFENCE`
#ASSERT `ss 46PI, 46PM -- must I give the information` TRUE 14 TRUE 15 TRUE FALSE EQUALS `I EXCUSE`
-- Not yet given, day 10 of 14: still to do.
#ASSERT `ss 46PI, 46PM -- must I give the information` TRUE 14 FALSE 10 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `I MUST`
#ASSERT `ss 46PI, 46PM -- must I give the information` TRUE 14 FALSE 14 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `I MUST`
-- Not given by day 20: an offence, unless self-incrimination or another reasonable excuse.
#ASSERT `ss 46PI, 46PM -- must I give the information` TRUE 14 FALSE 20 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `I OFFENCE`
#ASSERT `ss 46PI, 46PM -- must I give the information` TRUE 14 FALSE 20 FALSE TRUE EQUALS `I EXCUSE`
#ASSERT `ss 46PI, 46PM -- must I give the information` TRUE 14 FALSE 20 TRUE FALSE EQUALS `I EXCUSE`
-- Refusing on day 5 on the ground of self-incrimination: no offence.
#ASSERT `ss 46PI, 46PM -- must I give the information` TRUE 14 FALSE 5 FALSE TRUE EQUALS `I EXCUSE`
-- A request without a written notice under s 46PI.
#ASSERT `ss 46PI, 46PM -- must I give the information` FALSE 14 FALSE 20 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `I NO DUTY`

#ASSERT `s 46PN -- most months of imprisonment for false or misleading information` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST 6
#ASSERT `s 46PN -- most months of imprisonment for false or misleading information` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 46PN -- most months of imprisonment for false or misleading information` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `ss 46PJ, 46PK, 46PKA -- the conference`

`C MUST` MEANS `you must attend: failing to comply with the notice is a strict liability offence, 10 penalty units (s 46PJ(5), (6)); you are entitled to a reasonable sum from the Commonwealth for your expenses of attendance (s 46PJ(7))`
`C ATTENDED` MEANS `you attended as required: you are entitled to a reasonable sum from the Commonwealth for your expenses of attendance (s 46PJ(7))`
`C INVITED` MEANS `not compulsory: you were invited, not required by written notice; the offence needs a notice under s 46PJ(3) (s 46PJ(5)(a), the text's no)`
`C BAD NOTICE` MEANS `the notice does not meet s 46PJ(4) (a time less than 14 days after it was given, or no statement of the offence); the Act does not say whether it still binds you (NOTHING-kind, fork F4)`

-- Arguments: written notice, days of notice, states the offence, attended.
#ASSERT `s 46PJ -- must I attend the conference` TRUE 14 TRUE FALSE EQUALS `C MUST`
#ASSERT `s 46PJ -- must I attend the conference` TRUE 21 TRUE TRUE EQUALS `C ATTENDED`
-- 13 days: less than 14 days after the notice is given.
#ASSERT `s 46PJ -- must I attend the conference` TRUE 13 TRUE FALSE EQUALS `C BAD NOTICE`
#ASSERT `s 46PJ -- must I attend the conference` TRUE 30 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `C BAD NOTICE`
#ASSERT `s 46PJ -- must I attend the conference` FALSE 30 TRUE FALSE EQUALS `C INVITED`

`R CONSENT` MEANS `yes: the person presiding has consented to your being represented (s 46PK(4))`
`R CANNOT ATTEND` MEANS `yes: you cannot attend because of a disability, so you may nominate another person to attend instead of you (s 46PK(5))`
`R ASSIST` MEANS `no, but you may nominate another person to assist you at the conference, as the person presiding considers your disability stops you participating fully (s 46PK(6))`
`R NO` MEANS `no: unless the person presiding consents, you are not entitled to be represented at the conference by another person (s 46PK(4)(a), the text's no)`

#ASSERT `s 46PK -- may someone represent me at the conference` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `R CONSENT`
#ASSERT `s 46PK -- may someone represent me at the conference` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `R CANNOT ATTEND`
#ASSERT `s 46PK -- may someone represent me at the conference` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `R ASSIST`
#ASSERT `s 46PK -- may someone represent me at the conference` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `R NO`

#ASSERT `s 46PKA -- can what was said in conciliation be used` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: evidence of anything said or done in the conciliation is not admissible in proceedings about the acts complained of (s 46PKA(1), the text's no)`
#ASSERT `s 46PKA -- can what was said in conciliation be used` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes, it may be admitted: the bar does not apply when the court applies the costs rule in s 46PSA (s 46PKA(2))`
#ASSERT `s 46PKA -- can what was said in conciliation be used` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `s 46PKA does not deal with proceedings about other matters (NOTHING-kind)`

§ `s 46PH -- termination`

-- s 46PH(1)(b): the last day without the lateness ground.
#ASSERT `s 46PH(1)(b) -- the last day to lodge without the lateness ground` `15 Mar 2024` EQUALS `15 Mar 2026`
#ASSERT `s 46PH(1)(b) -- the last day to lodge without the lateness ground` `29 Feb 2024` EQUALS `28 Feb 2026`
#ASSERT `s 46PH(1)(b) -- the last day to lodge without the lateness ground` `31 Jan 2025` EQUALS `31 Jan 2027`
-- On the last day: not "more than 24 months after" (fork F2). The next day: more than.
#ASSERT (NOT (`lodged more than 24 months after the acts` `15 Mar 2024` `15 Mar 2026`))
#ASSERT `lodged more than 24 months after the acts` `15 Mar 2024` `16 Mar 2026`
#ASSERT (NOT (`lodged more than 24 months after the acts` `29 Feb 2024` `28 Feb 2026`))
#ASSERT `lodged more than 24 months after the acts` `29 Feb 2024` `1 Mar 2026`
-- Lodged within the 24 months (7 November 2025, about 20 months on), or dated before the acts: in time.
-- 7 November 2026 is more than 24 months after 15 March 2024.
#ASSERT `lodged more than 24 months after the acts` `15 Mar 2024` `7 Nov 2026`
#ASSERT (NOT (`lodged more than 24 months after the acts` `15 Mar 2024` `7 Nov 2025`))
#ASSERT (NOT (`lodged more than 24 months after the acts` `15 Mar 2024` `1 Jan 2024`))

`T MUST TRIVIAL` MEANS `the President must terminate it: trivial, vexatious, misconceived or lacking in substance (s 46PH(1B)(a))`
`T MUST NO CONCILIATION` MEANS `the President must terminate it: no reasonable prospect of settlement by conciliation (s 46PH(1B)(b)); you will not need the court's leave to apply (s 46PO(3A)(c))`
`T MUST NO COURT` MEANS `the President must terminate it: no reasonable prospect that the court would find unlawful discrimination (s 46PH(1C))`
`T MAY NOT UD` MEANS `the President may terminate it: not unlawful discrimination (s 46PH(1)(a))`
`T MAY LATE` MEANS `the President may terminate it: lodged more than 24 months after the acts (s 46PH(1)(b))`
`T MAY NOT WARRANTED` MEANS `the President may terminate it: an inquiry is not warranted (s 46PH(1)(c))`
`T MAY OTHER REMEDY` MEANS `the President may terminate it: another remedy sought has adequately dealt with it (s 46PH(1)(d))`
`T MAY BETTER REMEDY` MEANS `the President may terminate it: a more appropriate remedy is reasonably available to each affected person (s 46PH(1)(e))`
`T MAY DEALT WITH` MEANS `the President may terminate it: already adequately dealt with by the Commission or another statutory authority (s 46PH(1)(f))`
`T MAY OTHER AUTHORITY` MEANS `the President may terminate it: another statutory authority could deal with it more effectively or conveniently (s 46PH(1)(g))`
`T MAY PUBLIC IMPORTANCE` MEANS `the President may terminate it: an issue of public importance for the Federal Court or the Federal Circuit and Family Court (s 46PH(1)(h)); you will not need the court's leave to apply (s 46PO(3A)(b))`
`T NO GROUND` MEANS `no ground in s 46PH is made out on these facts; the President may still terminate without inquiry if of the opinion it should be terminated (s 46PF(1)(b)) (NOTHING-kind)`

-- Arguments: (1B)(a), (1B)(b), (1C), (1)(a), acts on, lodged on, (1)(c), (d), (e), (f), (g), (h).
#ASSERT `s 46PH -- can my complaint be terminated` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `15 Mar 2024` `15 Mar 2026` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `T NO GROUND`
#ASSERT `s 46PH -- can my complaint be terminated` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `15 Mar 2024` `16 Mar 2026` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `T MAY LATE`
#ASSERT `s 46PH -- can my complaint be terminated` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `15 Mar 2024` `7 Nov 2025` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `T MUST TRIVIAL`
-- A mandatory ground is reported before a discretionary one (late as well).
#ASSERT `s 46PH -- can my complaint be terminated` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `15 Mar 2024` `16 Mar 2026` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `T MUST NO CONCILIATION`
#ASSERT `s 46PH -- can my complaint be terminated` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `15 Mar 2024` `7 Nov 2025` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `T MUST NO COURT`
#ASSERT `s 46PH -- can my complaint be terminated` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE `15 Mar 2024` `7 Nov 2025` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `T MAY NOT UD`
#ASSERT `s 46PH -- can my complaint be terminated` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `15 Mar 2024` `7 Nov 2025` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `T MAY NOT WARRANTED`
#ASSERT `s 46PH -- can my complaint be terminated` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `15 Mar 2024` `7 Nov 2025` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `T MAY OTHER REMEDY`
#ASSERT `s 46PH -- can my complaint be terminated` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `15 Mar 2024` `7 Nov 2025` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `T MAY BETTER REMEDY`
#ASSERT `s 46PH -- can my complaint be terminated` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `15 Mar 2024` `7 Nov 2025` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `T MAY DEALT WITH`
#ASSERT `s 46PH -- can my complaint be terminated` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `15 Mar 2024` `7 Nov 2025` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `T MAY OTHER AUTHORITY`
#ASSERT `s 46PH -- can my complaint be terminated` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `15 Mar 2024` `7 Nov 2025` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `T MAY PUBLIC IMPORTANCE`

`NOTICE COMPLAINANT` MEANS `yes: as a complainant you must be notified in writing of the termination and the reasons, with a statement that the court can award costs in certain circumstances (s 46PH(2), (2A))`
`NOTICE COPY` MEANS `yes: as an affected person who is not a complainant, you must be given a copy of that notice because you asked for it (s 46PH(3))`
`NOTICE NO` MEANS `no: an affected person who is not a complainant is given a copy only on request (s 46PH(3), "on request": the text's no)`

#ASSERT `s 46PH(2), (3) -- must I be sent the termination notice` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `NOTICE COMPLAINANT`
#ASSERT `s 46PH(2), (3) -- must I be sent the termination notice` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `NOTICE COPY`
#ASSERT `s 46PH(2), (3) -- must I be sent the termination notice` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `NOTICE NO`

#ASSERT `s 46PH(4) -- may the President revoke the termination` FALSE
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 46PH(4) -- may the President revoke the termination` TRUE))

§ `ss 46PO, 46POB -- going to court`

`open` MEANS `it has not ended: the President is still dealing with it`
`withdrawn complaint` MEANS `it was withdrawn with the President's leave (s 46PG)`
`ended 46PE` MEANS `terminated on request, as a complaint against the Commission (s 46PE)`
`ended without inquiry` MEANS `terminated without inquiry (s 46PF(1)(b))`
`ended (1)(h)` MEANS `terminated: issue of public importance (s 46PH(1)(h))`
`ended (1B)(b)` MEANS `terminated: no reasonable prospect of conciliation (s 46PH(1B)(b))`
`ended other 46PH` MEANS `terminated on another ground in s 46PH`
`affected` MEANS `a person on whose behalf it was lodged (including lodging it myself)`
`lodger` MEANS `a person or trade union that lodged it for others`
`stranger` MEANS `neither`

`CT NO LEAVE NEEDED` MEANS `yes: you may apply to the Federal Court or the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2) without needing the court's leave, given the ground of termination (s 46PO(1), (3A)(b) or (c)); apply within 60 days of the notice (s 46PO(2))`
`CT WITH LEAVE` MEANS `yes: you may apply to the Federal Court or the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2) with the leave the court has granted (s 46PO(1), (3A)(a)); apply within 60 days of the notice (s 46PO(2))`
`CT LEAVE NEEDED` MEANS `no: on this ground of termination the application must not be made unless the court grants leave (s 46PO(3A), "must not ... unless": the text's no)`
`CT NOT ENDED` MEANS `no: an application may be made only after the President terminates the complaint and gives notice of it (s 46PO(1), "if": the text's no)`
`CT WITHDRAWN` MEANS `no: a withdrawn complaint is not a terminated complaint, so s 46PO does not open the way to court (s 46PO(1), "if": the text's no)`
`CT NO NOTICE` MEANS `no: the President has not yet given the written notice of termination (s 46PO(1)(b), "if": the text's no)`
`CT IN REP` MEANS `no: you are part of a representative application on the same subject matter and have not opted out (s 46POB(1), the text's no)`
`CT DIFFERENT` MEANS `no: the application must allege the same unlawful discrimination as the complaint, or discrimination arising out of the same acts (s 46PO(3), the text's no)`
`CT NOT LISTED` MEANS `s 46PO(2A) does not list you: the application is made by an affected person, or by the person or union that lodged the complaint (NOTHING-kind)`

-- Arguments: how it ended, notice given, who I am, same discrimination, court gave leave, in a representative application.
#ASSERT `s 46PO -- may I apply to the court` `ended (1B)(b)` TRUE `affected` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `CT NO LEAVE NEEDED`
#ASSERT `s 46PO -- may I apply to the court` `ended (1)(h)` TRUE `affected` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `CT NO LEAVE NEEDED`
#ASSERT `s 46PO -- may I apply to the court` `ended (1)(h)` TRUE `lodger` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `CT NO LEAVE NEEDED`
#ASSERT `s 46PO -- may I apply to the court` `ended other 46PH` TRUE `affected` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `CT LEAVE NEEDED`
#ASSERT `s 46PO -- may I apply to the court` `ended other 46PH` TRUE `affected` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `CT WITH LEAVE`
#ASSERT `s 46PO -- may I apply to the court` `ended without inquiry` TRUE `affected` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `CT LEAVE NEEDED`
#ASSERT `s 46PO -- may I apply to the court` `ended 46PE` TRUE `affected` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `CT WITH LEAVE`
#ASSERT `s 46PO -- may I apply to the court` `open` TRUE `affected` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `CT NOT ENDED`
#ASSERT `s 46PO -- may I apply to the court` `withdrawn complaint` TRUE `affected` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `CT WITHDRAWN`
#ASSERT `s 46PO -- may I apply to the court` `ended (1B)(b)` FALSE `affected` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `CT NO NOTICE`
#ASSERT `s 46PO -- may I apply to the court` `ended (1B)(b)` TRUE `stranger` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `CT NOT LISTED`
#ASSERT `s 46PO -- may I apply to the court` `ended (1B)(b)` TRUE `affected` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `CT IN REP`
#ASSERT `s 46PO -- may I apply to the court` `ended (1B)(b)` TRUE `affected` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `CT DIFFERENT`

-- s 46PO(2): 60 days after the date of issue.
#ASSERT `s 46PO(2) -- the last day to apply to the court` `1 Oct 2026` EQUALS `30 Nov 2026`
-- 2 January 2026 plus 60 days: 29 days left in January, 28 in February, so 3 March 2026.
#ASSERT `s 46PO(2) -- the last day to apply to the court` `2 Jan 2026` EQUALS `3 Mar 2026`
-- A leap year: 1 January 2024 plus 60 days is 1 March 2024.
#ASSERT `s 46PO(2) -- the last day to apply to the court` `1 Jan 2024` EQUALS `1 Mar 2024`

`AP IN TIME` MEANS `in time: made within 60 days after the date of issue of the termination notice (s 46PO(2))`
`AP EXTENDED` MEANS `out of time, but within the further time the court has allowed (s 46PO(2))`
`AP LATE` MEANS `out of time: it must be made within 60 days after the date of issue of the notice, or such further time as the court allows (s 46PO(2), the text's no)`

#ASSERT `s 46PO(2) -- is my court application in time` `1 Oct 2026` `30 Nov 2026` FALSE EQUALS `AP IN TIME`
#ASSERT `s 46PO(2) -- is my court application in time` `1 Oct 2026` `1 Oct 2026` FALSE EQUALS `AP IN TIME`
#ASSERT `s 46PO(2) -- is my court application in time` `1 Oct 2026` `7 Nov 2026` FALSE EQUALS `AP IN TIME`
-- Day 61: late.
#ASSERT `s 46PO(2) -- is my court application in time` `1 Oct 2026` `1 Dec 2026` FALSE EQUALS `AP LATE`
#ASSERT `s 46PO(2) -- is my court application in time` `1 Oct 2026` `1 Dec 2026` TRUE EQUALS `AP EXTENDED`
#ASSERT `s 46PO(2) -- is my court application in time` `1 Oct 2026` `30 Nov 2026` TRUE EQUALS `AP IN TIME`
#ASSERT `s 46PO(2) -- is my court application in time` `2 Jan 2026` `3 Mar 2026` FALSE EQUALS `AP IN TIME`
#ASSERT `s 46PO(2) -- is my court application in time` `2 Jan 2026` `15 Mar 2026` FALSE EQUALS `AP LATE`

-- s 46PO(4): seven kinds of order when the court is satisfied; none otherwise.
#ASSERT count (`s 46PO(4) -- what the court can order` TRUE) EQUALS 7
#ASSERT count (`s 46PO(4) -- what the court can order` FALSE) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT elem `an order to employ or re-employ you (s 46PO(4)(c))` (`s 46PO(4) -- what the court can order` TRUE)
#ASSERT elem `an order to pay you damages as compensation for loss or damage caused by the respondent's conduct, with no cap in the Act (s 46PO(4)(d))` (`s 46PO(4) -- what the court can order` TRUE)

#ASSERT `ss 46PB(4), 46POA -- is my consent needed` `a representative complaint to the Commission` EQUALS `no: a representative complaint may be lodged without the consent of class members (s 46PB(4)); you may withdraw from it by written notice before it is terminated (s 46PC(1))`
#ASSERT `ss 46PB(4), 46POA -- is my consent needed` `a representative application to the court under s 46PO` EQUALS `yes: a representative application may not be made without your written consent (s 46POA(1), the text's no); you may also opt out by the date the court fixes (s 46POB(3))`
#ASSERT `ss 46PB(4), 46POA -- is my consent needed` `a representative proceeding in the Federal Court under Part IVA of the Federal Court of Australia Act 1976` EQUALS `this Act does not say: a Part IVA proceeding is governed by the Federal Court of Australia Act 1976 (s 3(1) representative application; NOTHING-kind)`

`O YES` MEANS `yes: you may opt out by written notice to the court before the date it fixed (s 46POB(3)); you may then make your own application (s 46POB(1))`
`O MAKER` MEANS `no: the person who made the representative application cannot opt out of it (s 46POB(3), "other than": the text's no)`
`O LATE` MEANS `no: opting out must be before the date the court fixed, or extended (s 46POB(3)(a), a period the text fixes: the text's no)`
`O NO NOTICE` MEANS `not yet: opting out is by written notice to the court, in accordance with its rules (s 46POB(3)) (NOTHING-kind)`

#ASSERT `s 46POB -- may I opt out` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `O YES`
#ASSERT `s 46POB -- may I opt out` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `O NO NOTICE`
#ASSERT `s 46POB -- may I opt out` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `O LATE`
#ASSERT `s 46POB -- may I opt out` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `O MAKER`

§ `ss 46PP, 46PO(6) -- interim injunctions`

`J STATUS QUO` MEANS `yes: you may ask the court for an interim injunction to keep things as they were before you complained, or to protect your rights, and you cannot be made to give an undertaking as to damages (s 46PP(1), (2), (5))`
`J PENDING` MEANS `yes: the court may grant an interim injunction pending the determination of your proceedings, without requiring an undertaking as to damages (s 46PO(6), (8))`
`J NOT LODGED` MEANS `no: an interim injunction under s 46PP is available only after a complaint is lodged (s 46PP(1), a period the text fixes: the text's no)`
`J ENDED` MEANS `no: an interim injunction under s 46PP cannot be granted after the complaint is withdrawn or terminated (s 46PP(3), the text's no)`

#ASSERT `ss 46PP, 46PO(6) -- can I ask for an interim injunction` `not yet lodged` EQUALS `J NOT LODGED`
#ASSERT `ss 46PP, 46PO(6) -- can I ask for an interim injunction` `lodged and still with the President` EQUALS `J STATUS QUO`
#ASSERT `ss 46PP, 46PO(6) -- can I ask for an interim injunction` `withdrawn` EQUALS `J ENDED`
#ASSERT `ss 46PP, 46PO(6) -- can I ask for an interim injunction` `terminated, with no court application yet` EQUALS `J ENDED`
#ASSERT `ss 46PP, 46PO(6) -- can I ask for an interim injunction` `terminated, and I have applied to the court under s 46PO` EQUALS `J PENDING`

§ `ss 46PQ, 46PU -- representation and help`

#ASSERT `s 46PQ -- may they represent me in court` `I appear myself` FALSE EQUALS `yes: you may appear in person (s 46PQ(1)(a))`
-- The court's opinion matters only for a non-lawyer.
#ASSERT `s 46PQ -- may they represent me in court` `a barrister or solicitor` TRUE EQUALS `yes: you may be represented by a barrister or solicitor (s 46PQ(1)(b))`
#ASSERT `s 46PQ -- may they represent me in court` `another person who is not a barrister or solicitor` FALSE EQUALS `yes: you may be represented by a person who is not a lawyer, who may not demand or receive any fee, reward or expenses for it (s 46PQ(1)(c), (2))`
#ASSERT `s 46PQ -- may they represent me in court` `another person who is not a barrister or solicitor` TRUE EQUALS `no: the court is of the opinion that it is inappropriate for that person to appear (s 46PQ(1)(c), "unless": fork F3)`

`H YES` MEANS `yes, it may be given: the Attorney-General may authorise legal or financial assistance from the Commonwealth, on conditions the Attorney-General sets (s 46PU(2)); the Commission may also help you prepare the forms (s 46PT)`
`H NO` MEANS `no: the Attorney-General may authorise assistance only if satisfied that refusing would cause you hardship and that granting it is reasonable in all the circumstances (s 46PU(2), "if": the text's no); the Commission may still help you prepare the forms (s 46PT)`
`H NO PROCEEDINGS` MEANS `no: assistance under s 46PU is for a person who has started or proposes to start proceedings under Part IIB Division 2 (s 46PU(1), the text's no)`

#ASSERT `s 46PU -- can I get help with my court case` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `H YES`
#ASSERT `s 46PU -- can I get help with my court case` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `H NO`
#ASSERT `s 46PU -- can I get help with my court case` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `H NO`
#ASSERT `s 46PU -- can I get help with my court case` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `H NO PROCEEDINGS`

§ `s 46PSA -- costs`

`RC YES` MEANS `yes: the court must order the respondent to pay your costs, and may order them assessed on an indemnity basis (s 46PSA(2), (3))`
`RC EXCEPT` MEANS `yes, except: the court must order the respondent to pay your costs, but need not order it to pay the costs your own unreasonable act or omission caused you (s 46PSA(2), (4))`
`RC LOST` MEANS `no: s 46PSA(2) requires a costs order only against a respondent against whom you succeed on one or more grounds ("if": the text's no)`
`RC NOT APPLY` MEANS `s 46PSA does not apply: it covers proceedings, including appeals, relating to an application to the court under s 46PO (s 46PSA(1), a scope limit: NOTHING-kind)`

#ASSERT `s 46PSA -- must the respondent pay my costs` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `RC YES`
#ASSERT `s 46PSA -- must the respondent pay my costs` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `RC EXCEPT`
#ASSERT `s 46PSA -- must the respondent pay my costs` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `RC LOST`
#ASSERT `s 46PSA -- must the respondent pay my costs` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `RC NOT APPLY`

`maker` MEANS `I made the application (alone, or as the person who made a representative application)`
`group member` MEANS `a representative application was made on my behalf by someone else`

`AC NO` MEANS `no: you must not be ordered to pay another party's costs (s 46PSA(5), the text's no)`
`AC REP` MEANS `no: in a representative application, costs cannot be awarded against a person on whose behalf it was made, other than the person who made it (s 46PSA(7), with (5): the text's no)`
`AC VEXATIOUS` MEANS `you may be ordered to pay: the court is satisfied you brought the proceedings vexatiously or without reasonable cause (s 46PSA(6)(a))`
`AC CONDUCT` MEANS `you may be ordered to pay the costs your unreasonable act or omission caused the other party (s 46PSA(6)(b))`
`AC EQUALS` MEANS `you may be ordered to pay: the respondent succeeded and has neither a significant power advantage over you nor significantly greater financial or other resources (s 46PSA(6)(c))`
`AC NOT APPLY` MEANS `s 46PSA does not apply, so this Act does not say: it covers proceedings, including appeals, relating to an application to the court under s 46PO (s 46PSA(1), a scope limit: NOTHING-kind)`

-- Arguments: s 46PO case, my place, vexatious, unreasonable conduct, respondent succeeded, power advantage, more resources.
-- An employee loses against a large employer: protected (s 46PSA(5)); (6)(c) fails on (ii) and (iii).
#ASSERT `s 46PSA -- can I be made to pay their costs` TRUE `maker` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `AC NO`
-- Loses against a respondent with a power advantage only: (6)(c)(ii) fails.
#ASSERT `s 46PSA -- can I be made to pay their costs` TRUE `maker` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `AC NO`
-- Loses against a respondent with more resources only: (6)(c)(iii) fails.
#ASSERT `s 46PSA -- can I be made to pay their costs` TRUE `maker` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `AC NO`
-- Loses against an individual respondent of equal standing: (6)(c) met.
#ASSERT `s 46PSA -- can I be made to pay their costs` TRUE `maker` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `AC EQUALS`
-- Wins (the respondent did not succeed) against an equal respondent: (6)(c)(i) fails.
#ASSERT `s 46PSA -- can I be made to pay their costs` TRUE `maker` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `AC NO`
#ASSERT `s 46PSA -- can I be made to pay their costs` TRUE `maker` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `AC VEXATIOUS`
#ASSERT `s 46PSA -- can I be made to pay their costs` TRUE `maker` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `AC CONDUCT`
-- A person in a representative application who did not make it: protected even where (6)(a) would apply.
#ASSERT `s 46PSA -- can I be made to pay their costs` TRUE `group member` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `AC REP`
#ASSERT `s 46PSA -- can I be made to pay their costs` FALSE `maker` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `AC NOT APPLY`
